# Code quality

- Prefer clean, readable, maintainable code over clever shortcuts.
- Avoid unnecessary comments; comment only non-obvious logic, business rules, or constraints.
- Reuse existing helpers/modules; extract shared logic instead of copy-paste.
- Avoid unnecessary duplication.
- Apply SOLID when it clearly improves the design (e.g. splitting a god service). Do not lecture SOLID on every change.
- Follow NestJS module/layer conventions in this repo (controller → service → data).
